# Testing Policy

## Strategy SSOT

Pyramid, waves, and module priorities: `@docs/05-plans/testing-strategy.md`.
Measured coverage numbers: `@docs/05-plans/testing-baseline.md`.
How-to: `@.cursor/skills/testing/SKILL.md`, patterns: `@.cursor/skills/testing/PATTERNS.md`.

## When shipping a feature

Domain agents own layer-appropriate tests with the feature. Do **not** default to unit-only.

| Change | Add / update |
|--------|----------------|
| Pure logic `engine/` `shared/` utils / extracted helpers | Co-located `*.test.ts` (`npm run test`) |
| Preact component / hook / page | `*.test.tsx` / `*.hook.test.ts` (`npm run test:component`); page smoke OK |
| New/changed Express route wiring | `tests/integration/api/*.test.ts` (`npm run test:integration`) |
| Client↔server enum / critical request shape **not** already covered by thorough Zod unit | `tests/contracts/**` (`npm run test:contract`) |
| Deferred monster / `ProjectInfo` (`COMPONENT_DEFERRED` in gaps) | Extract + unit; **do not** full-mount |

**Contract selectivity:** prefer enum-sync and high-value / high-churn request bodies. Do **not** duplicate exhaustive Zod unit suites with fixture spam.

**Agent routing:** domain agents write these layer tests; Testing utility owns infra, `test:gaps` campaigns, and cross-layer work.

## Runner and layout

- **Pin:** Vitest + `@vitest/coverage-v8` exact **`5.0.0`** (no `^`). Windows wrappers (`scripts/test-*.mjs`, explicit file lists, `maxWorkers: 2`, no integration `setupFiles`) stay until Windows + Node 24 proof that glob/dir entry and `setupFiles` work on 5.x.
- **Vitest 5 `exclude`:** v5 `defaultExclude` is only `node_modules` + `.git` (no `dist/**`). Custom `test.exclude` **replaces** defaults — spread `configDefaults.exclude`, then add `**/dist/**`, `tests/e2e/**`, and layer splits. Unit must keep `src/**/*.hook.test.ts` out (`*.hook.test.ts` matches `*.test.ts`).
- **Component pool:** `forks` (Vitest 5 default). Do not set `pool: 'threads'` — Node `fetch` in worker_threads can hang the suite ([vitest#3077](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/3077)). Hang log: `@docs/05-plans/coverage-campaign-extracts.md`.
- **Runner:** Vitest via wrappers where needed:
  - `npm run test` → `scripts/test-unit.mjs` (native cwd casing + hoisted vitest)
  - `npm run test:component` → `scripts/test-component.mjs` (explicit file list)
  - `npm run test:integration` → `scripts/test-integration.mjs` (explicit file list)
  - Also: `test:slow`, `test:contract`, `test:all`, `test:coverage`, `test:component:coverage`, `test:contract:coverage`, `test:gaps`
  - Local E2E (not pre-push): `test:e2e` (Playwright Chromium, invert `@llm` and `@visual`), `test:e2e:visual` (pixel shells), `test:e2e:llm` (includes live OpenAI)
- **Configs:** `@vitest.config.ts` (unit + coverage floors), `@vitest.slow.config.ts`, `@vitest.component.config.ts` (happy-dom, Preact JSX, CLIENT_SCOPE coverage), `@vitest.contract.config.ts` (Zod fixtures + advisory schema coverage), `@vitest.integration.config.ts` (forks, **no** `setupFiles`), `@playwright.config.ts` (local E2E; pin `@playwright/test` **1.63.0**)
- **File naming:** co-located `foo.test.ts` / `foo.test.tsx` next to source (not `.spec.ts`). Hook Testing Library suites may use `*.hook.test.ts`. Integration/contract live under `tests/`. Local E2E specs use `*.spec.ts` under `tests/e2e/specs/`; locators only via `tests/e2e/targets/` (Persona/Actor; see `@.cursor/skills/testing/PATTERNS.md`). Pixel shells only in `*.visual.spec.ts` via `layoutMatches` (`fullPage`; phone 390 / tablet **834** / desktop 1280 CSS viewports — tablet is inside 768–1023, not on the 768 boundary); fixture seeds dismissed alerts so the banner is out of the shot.
- **Imports:** NodeNext — use `.js` extensions in test imports (same as production code).
- **Wrappers allowed:** `scripts/test-*.mjs` / `scripts/resolve-vitest.mjs` for runner workarounds only — not for test cases. Put tests under `src/**/*.test.ts(x)` or `tests/`. Inventory helpers `scripts/gen-test-inventory.mjs` and `scripts/gen-layer-gaps.mjs` are allowed.

## APP_SCOPE (unified)

Same scope for unit tests, coverage, and Stryker `mutate`:

- `src/**/*.ts` minus `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` / `*.hook.test.ts`, `src/debug-app/**`, `src/prompt-lab-app/**`, `src/debug/**`, `src/prompt-lab/**`
- Includes **backend + client SPA**

SSOT: `@vitest.config.ts`, `@stryker.conf.json`. Baseline: `@docs/05-plans/testing-baseline.md`.

## Test environment

**Default (pre-push and GitHub Actions):** mock external boundaries for unit, component, mock-integration, and contract tests. Tests must not require prod/staging `.env` credentials.

| Term in Arcane | Means |
|----------------|-------|
| Unit test | co-located `*.test.ts`; `vi.mock` at DB/LLM/HTTP boundaries |
| Component test | `@testing-library/preact` + happy-dom; mocked `fetch` / hooks |
| Integration test (mock) | `createApp()` + supertest; mocked Supabase/Redis/LLM |
| Local E2E (Wave 10) | Playwright Chromium vs Docker stamp (`stack:up` / `stack:restore` + `dev`). **Not** pre-push / GitHub Actions |
| Integration test (live CI) | **Still blocked** — dedicated CI test stack / `tests/integration/supabase/` |

**Local E2E (unblocked):** personas are seed users from `supabase/seed.sql` (`user@` / `author@` / `author-plus@` / `admin@local.test`, password `local-dev-password`). Stamp remaps dump owners to Author; Reader owns **0** projects. Live OpenAI only in `@llm`. Actor/Persona SSOT: `@.cursor/skills/testing/PATTERNS.md` + `@tests/e2e/README.md`. Fail loudly if stamp/dev is missing — do not `exit 0`.

**CI docker-compose / live Supabase integration:** still Q4 blocked. Never E2E against prod/staging UI.

See `@docs/05-plans/testing-strategy.md`.

## Layer obligation (do not substitute)

| Situation | Layer / command |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Pure logic / Zod / handlers with mocks | Co-located unit (`npm run test`) |
| Preact UI / hooks | `npm run test:component` (`*.test.tsx` / `*.hook.test.ts`) |
| Presentational markup (`ui/*`, EntityCard, TagChip) | `toMatchSnapshot` in component suite — update `.snap` intentionally in the same PR |
| HTTP middleware order / status wiring / job runner | `tests/integration/**` mock-first (`npm run test:integration`) |
| Bug fix in pure logic (`engine/`, `shared/`, utils) | Regression in co-located `*.test.ts` |
| Live LLM / OpenAI API | **Never** in unit/component/mock-integration — mock provider. Local E2E: only `@llm` (`npm run test:e2e:llm`) |
| Live Supabase (local stamp) | Playwright `tests/e2e/**` after `stack:up` / `stack:restore` — Testing utility; **not** a substitute for component/mock-integration |
| Live Supabase / Redis / BullMQ in CI | **Still blocked** — dedicated test environment |

Do **not** use unit tests as a substitute for mock-integration wiring checks, or vice versa. Do **not** snapshot full pages, `ReadingMode`, Auth gates, or async-loaded DOM. Do **not** write E2E instead of the layer in “When shipping a feature”.

## Test types in Arcane

| Type | Pre-push | GitHub Actions | Local / Q4 |
|------|----------|----------------|------------|
| Unit | `npm run test` | `npm run test:coverage` (floors) | same |
| Component | yes | yes | same |
| Integration (mock) | yes | yes | keep as fast CI layer |
| Integration (live) | — | — | dedicated stack still blocked |
| Snapshot | via component suite | via component suite | same |
| Contract | yes | yes | OpenAPI / Pact after split |
| System/E2E | no | no | **local stamp unblocked** (`npm run test:e2e`); Playwright-as-gate still blocked |

## Layer boundaries

| Layer | Allowed in tests (Q3) | Forbidden |
|-------|----------------------|-----------|
| `src/engine/**` | Pure pipeline, glossary, prompts, mocked LLM | HTTP, Supabase, `req.log` |
| `src/shared/**` | Pure utilities, business rules | DB, Redis |
| `src/api/**` | `validateRoute` helpers, Zod; mocked middleware | Full Express app without mocks (use `createApp` + mocks in `tests/integration`) |
| `src/client/**` | URL builders, hooks, components with mocked `fetch` | Live API without mocks |
| `src/services/**` | extracted pure helpers with mocks | live `supabaseDatabase` calls |
| `src/createApp.ts` | mock-integration via supertest | listen() in tests |

## Mutation testing (manual)

- Command: `npm run test:mutation` or zone smoke `npx stryker run --mutate <glob>`
- Scope: APP_SCOPE `src/**/*.ts` minus tests and lab apps (same as unit coverage include). **Does not mutate `.tsx`** — client components live in the component suite, not Stryker's Vitest unit runner.
- Mutate excludes `*.test.ts`, `*.test.tsx`, and `*.hook.test.ts` (hook suites were matching `*.ts` and must stay out of mutate).
- Dry-run uses `vitest.config.ts` with `related: false` (full unit suite once to build perTest coverage). Smoke on one file still pays that dry-run.
- **Not** in CI or pre-push; manual/nightly only
- `thresholds.high: 80`, `low: 60`, **`break: null`** — advisory bands / trend only, not a merge gate
- Reports: `reports/mutation/mutation.html`, `reports/mutation/mutation.json`
- **TypeScript 7 workaround:** keep `tsconfig.json` in `stryker.conf.json` `ignorePatterns`. Stryker 10.0.0 `TSConfigPreprocessor` still calls `ts.parseConfigFileTextToJson`, which TS7 removed ([stryker-js#6111](https://github.com/stryker-mutator/stryker-js/issues/6111)). Safe here: flat tsconfig, Vitest/esbuild, no typescript-checker. Remove the pattern when Stryker ships the jsonc-parser fix.
- **Node for Babel 8:** Stryker 10 instruments via `@babel/core@8`, which declares `^22.18.0 || >=24.11.0`. Local Node 24.10 may warn `EBADENGINE`; install with `npm install --no-workspaces --engine-strict=false`. Prefer Node **24.11+** for mutation runs. `.nvmrc` stays `24` (CI `setup-node` uses latest 24.x).

## Gates

- Before **commit:** pre-commit runs lint-staged only (fast).
- Before **push:** `npm run lint:all`, `npm run test`, `npm run test:component`, `npm run test:integration`, and `npm run test:contract` (enforced via `.husky/pre-push`). **`test:e2e` is not a push/merge gate.**
- **GitHub Actions** (`.github/workflows/test.yml`): `lint:all` + `test:coverage` (floors) + `test:component` + `test:integration` + `test:contract`. No Playwright, no `test:gaps`, no mutation.
- Husky hooks source `.husky/load-node.sh` so GUI Git (Cursor, VS Code) can find nvm/Homebrew `node`/`npx`/`npm`.
- **Coverage floors:** `npm run test:coverage` enforces `coverage.thresholds` in `@vitest.config.ts` (lines **77**, branches **65** — measured floors). **CI merge gate; not in pre-push.**
- Local E2E (`test:e2e` / `:visual` / `:llm`) is machine-local against the Docker stamp. Never a merge gate.
- If a PR drops below floors, fix tests or adjust floors **deliberately** in the same PR (never silent lower).

## Coverage policy

- Floors on `test:coverage` (GitHub Actions merge gate; not pre-push); track trend above floors.
- Prioritize `engine/` and `shared/` pure modules; expand to client components/hooks and mock-integration.
- Baseline: `@docs/05-plans/testing-baseline.md`. Strategy: `@docs/05-plans/testing-strategy.md`.

## Layer gaps (component + contract)

- **Command:** `npm run test:gaps` → runs component suite with coverage (or `--reuse`), then writes `reports/layer-gaps.json`.
- **Component:** presence (co-located `*.test.tsx` / `*.hook.test.ts`) + v8 on CLIENT_SCOPE (`coverage-component/`). Deferred UI monsters are listed, not counted as gaps.
- **Contract:** schema export inventory vs `tests/contracts/**` mentions + enum-sync manifest. Line % is advisory only (`test:contract:coverage`).
- **Not** merged into unit APP_SCOPE floors. **Not** in pre-push. Exit always 0 (advisory).

## Documentation workflow

When changing runner, gates, or test conventions:

1. Update this rule (`testing.mdc`) and `@.cursor/skills/testing/SKILL.md`.
2. Mirror to `@docs/_canonical/rules/testing.mdc`.
3. Update `@docs/05-plans/testing-strategy.md` / baseline if waves or scripts change.
4. Update `@AGENTS.md` commands table if scripts change.

## Agent routing

- Feature code + **layer-appropriate tests** → domain agent (Engine/API/Backend/UI) — choose layer from “When shipping a feature” above. Domain agents are **not** required to add Playwright specs with every feature.
- Test infrastructure, migration, coverage baseline, gap campaigns, **`tests/e2e/**` + `playwright.config.ts`** → **Testing** utility (`@.cursor/agents/testing/AGENT.md`).
- **verifier** runs `lint:all` + suites for changed layers (`test` / `test:component` / `test:integration` / `test:contract`). Does **not** run `test:e2e`.
